  "title": "An App Designer record save deletes and re-inserts the PSRECDEFN row and every PSRECFIELD and PSRECFIELDDB row of the record",
  "statement": "On Save, App Designer physically rewrites the record: the PSRECDEFN row and every PSRECFIELD and PSRECFIELDDB row get new ROWIDs, changed or not. Inferred from flashback ROWID diffs. Stamps are not part of this claim: across the single-save record captures most unchanged rows kept LASTUPDDTTM (202 of 204), but rows whose USEEDIT / USEEDIT2 bits App Designer set itself from a record-level setting (Timestamp Field Auto-Update, In-Memory) also kept it, so \"restamped exactly when changed\" does not hold.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "compatibility": {
    "observedReleases": [
      "8.62.09"
    ],
    "knownIncompatible": []
  },
